<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51516" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zanclē</span></b> , ēs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζάγκλη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an older name of the
				city of Messana</i> (<i>Messina</i>), <i>in Sicily</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 290</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 1,
			662</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zanclaeus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Zancle</i>, <i>Zanclean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harena,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Sicily</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 729</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zanclēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
			Zancle</i>, <i>Zanclean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moenia,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Messana</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 48</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					14, 47</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
